1027: a second swap slot (kern.sweet_fb_queue2, default off) and Brightness_Scale on the framebuffer.

With async commits (1022) a swap arriving while another is pending held CoreAnimation's display thread in SwapEnd (1023)
until the vsync tick took the pending one; that wait ended just after the next tick, which CoreAnimation then missed:
frames whose encode + GPU work take longer than one refresh were shown every other refresh (30 fps). With the sysctl
set, the second swap waits in a second slot, promoted when the pending one is taken. Brightness_Scale (int, 16.16,
1.0): CoreAnimation reads it at every frame, and kern_CopyProperty syslogged it as not found each time. Applies after 1026.

